  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The maximum and the minimum equivalent resistance&nbsp;obtained by combining&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;identical resistors of resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>, are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;respectively. The ratio&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is equal to</p>\r"
